# ==== TREEBEARD EXAMPLE CONFIG ==============================================
# File:     governor
# Install:  $TREEBEARD_ETC/governor   (default TREEBEARD_ETC=/etc/treebeard; owner root:treebeard 0640)
# Status:   REQUIRED (fail-closed)
# Absent:   if unreadable or not exactly one valid agent name, the governor cannot be established and EVERY agent is denied model access.
# Read by:  will.py (gate resolution; Will deferred, not in this release)
# Values:   structural: one bare agent name
# ===========================================================================
# Canonical governor agent. ONE bare agent name, comments/blank lines ignored.
# Independent of agent_policy.conf by design: the governor keeps all model-
# routing gates even if ordinary-agent policy is malformed or unreadable.
# If THIS file cannot be read or does not name exactly one valid agent, the
# governor cannot be established and every agent is denied. No guessing.
treebeard
